WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.848
[MUSIC]

00:00:06.848 --> 00:00:10.790
I think we often see leadership
development as self development.

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:12.650
There's the individual level.

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:15.260
That's where we're really
thinking about you as a person.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:21.390
You know, a good leader understands what
she has to do to make herself develop,

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:23.290
but there's a second level.

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:24.990
That's the organizational level.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:32.570
A great leader understands and does what
she has to do to help others to develop.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:37.143
Most leaders are not
running entire companies.

00:00:37.143 --> 00:00:40.990
Most leaders are touching
only a handful of people.

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:45.560
Maybe they don't have any
formal leadership authority but

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:49.560
they do touch their peers and
their colleagues at work.

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:53.190
And those interactions
are opportunities to show leadership.

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:59.010
All of us are challenged
to engage in behaviors that

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:02.860
essentially have leadership
implications for the people around us.

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:09.979
How do your actions as a leader
affect the growth mindset of others?

00:01:09.979 --> 00:01:11.047
And then finally,

00:01:11.047 --> 00:01:14.921
the third level of analysis is
the environment of the organization,

00:01:14.921 --> 00:01:19.960
these includes, society, economy, the
broader culture, the natural environment.

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:23.490
The things each of us do at
work not only matters for

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:26.890
work, they also matter for
the broader world.

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:30.943
Because our actions as leaders,
in order for us to be exceptional,

00:01:30.943 --> 00:01:33.943
also will have implications
at that third level.

00:01:33.943 --> 00:01:36.381
[MUSIC]

00:01:36.381 --> 00:01:42.080
&gt;&gt; Expand your horizons and explore new
ways to elevate your leadership skills.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.638
Explore Stanford's upcoming programs.

00:01:44.638 --> 00:01:48.738
[MUSIC]

